\fBOutgoingMessage (extends Writable)\fR
The parent class of `ClientRequest` and `ServerResponse`. It is an abstract outgoing message from the perspective of the participants of an HTTP transaction.
.TP
\fBheaders()\fR
An object of the outgoing message headers. This is equivalent to `getHeaders()`
.TP
\fBwritableEnded()\fR
`true` if the write state is "ended"
.TP
\fBwritableFinished()\fR
`true` if the write state is "finished"
.TP
\fBwritableLength()\fR
The number of buffered bytes.
.TP
\fBwritableHighWaterMark()\fR
The `highWaterMark` of the writable stream.
.TP
\fBdestroy(err)\fR
Destroys the message. Once a socket is associated with the message and is connected, that socket will be destroyed as well.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIerr\fR (Error?; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIOutgoingMessage\fR
.TP
\fBend(chunk, encoding, callback)\fR
Finishes the outgoing message.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIchunk\fR (Buffer \\| Uint8Array \\| string \\| function; optional; default null)
.br
\fIencoding\fR (string \\| function; optional; default null)
.br
\fIcallback\fR (function; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIOutgoingMessage\fR
.TP
\fBappendHeader(name, value)\fR
Append a single header value for the header object.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIname\fR (string; required)
.br
\fIvalue\fR (string \\| string[]; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIOutgoingMessage\fR
.TP
\fBsetHeader(name, value)\fR
Set a single header value for the header object, replacing any existing value.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIname\fR (string; required)
.br
\fIvalue\fR (string; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIOutgoingMessage\fR
.TP
\fBflushHeaders()\fR
Flushes the message headers.
.TP
\fBgetHeader(name)\fR
Gets the value of the HTTP header with the given name. If that header is not set, the returned value will be `undefined`.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIname\fR (string; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIstring \\| undefined\fR
.TP
\fBgetHeaderNames()\fR
Returns an array containing the unique names of the current outgoing headers. All names are lowercase.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIstring[]\fR
.TP
\fBgetHeaders()\fR
Returns a copy of the HTTP headers as an object.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIobject\fR
.TP
\fBhasHeader(name)\fR
Returns true if the header identified by name is currently set in the outgoing headers. The header name is case\-insensitive.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIname\fR (string; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIboolean\fR
.TP
\fBremoveHeader(name)\fR
Removes a header that is queued for implicit sending.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIname\fR (string; required)
.TP
\fBsetTimeout(timeout, callback)\fR
Sets the outgoing message timeout with an optional callback.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fItimeout\fR (number; required)
.br
\fIcallback\fR (function; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIOutgoingMessage\fR
.TP
\fBIncomingMessage (extends Readable)\fR
An `IncomingMessage` object is created by `Server` or `ClientRequest` and passed as the first argument to the 'request' and 'response' event respectively. It may be used to access response status, headers, and data.
.TP
\fBserver()\fR
Documented method exposed by this module.
.TP
\fBcontext()\fR
Documented method exposed by this module.
.TP
\fBcomplete()\fR
This property will be `true` if a complete HTTP message has been received and successfully parsed.
.TP
\fBheaders()\fR
An object of the incoming message headers.
.TP
\fBurl()\fR
The URL for this incoming message. This value is not absolute with respect to the protocol and hostname. It includes the path and search query component parameters.
.TP
\fBheadersDistinct()\fR
Similar to `message.headers`, but there is no join logic and the values are always arrays of strings, even for headers received just once.
.TP
\fBhttpVersionMajor()\fR
The HTTP major version of this request.
.TP
\fBhttpVersionMinor()\fR
The HTTP minor version of this request.
.TP
\fBhttpVersion()\fR
The HTTP version string. A concatenation of `httpVersionMajor` and `httpVersionMinor`.
.TP
\fBmethod()\fR
The HTTP request method.
.TP
\fBrawHeaders()\fR
The raw request/response headers list potentially as they were received.
.TP
\fBstatusCode()\fR
The HTTP request status code. Only valid for response obtained from `ClientRequest`.
.TP
\fBstatusMessage()\fR
The HTTP response status message (reason phrase). Such as "OK" or "Internal Server Error." Only valid for response obtained from `ClientRequest`.
.TP
\fBstatus()\fR
An alias for `statusCode`
.TP
\fBstatusText()\fR
An alias for `statusMessage`
.TP
\fBgetHeader(name)\fR
Gets the value of the HTTP header with the given name. If that header is not set, the returned value will be `undefined`.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIname\fR (string; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIstring \\| undefined\fR
.TP
\fBgetHeaderNames()\fR
Returns an array containing the unique names of the current outgoing headers. All names are lowercase.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIstring[]\fR
.TP
\fBgetHeaders()\fR
Returns a copy of the HTTP headers as an object.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIobject\fR
.TP
\fBhasHeader(name)\fR
Returns true if the header identified by name is currently set in the outgoing headers. The header name is case\-insensitive.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIname\fR (string; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIboolean\fR
.TP
\fBsetTimeout(timeout, callback)\fR
Sets the incoming message timeout with an optional callback.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fItimeout\fR (number; required)
.br
\fIcallback\fR (function; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIIncomingMessage\fR
.TP
\fBClientRequest (extends OutgoingMessage)\fR
An object that is created internally and returned from `request()`.
.TP
\fBmethod()\fR
The HTTP request method.
.TP
\fBprotocol()\fR
The request protocol
.TP
\fBpath()\fR
The request path.
.TP
\fBhost()\fR
The request host name (including port).
.TP
\fBurl()\fR
The URL for this outgoing message. This value is not absolute with respect to the protocol and hostname. It includes the path and search query component parameters.
.TP
\fBServerResponse (extends OutgoingMessage)\fR
An object that is created internally by a `Server` instance, not by the user. It is passed as the second parameter to the 'request' event.
.TP
\fBconstructor(options)\fR
`ServerResponse` class constructor.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (object; required)
.TP
\fBserver()\fR
Documented method exposed by this module.
.TP
\fBrequest()\fR
A reference to the original HTTP request object.
.TP
\fBreq()\fR
A reference to the original HTTP request object.
.TP
\fBstatusCode()\fR
The HTTP request status code. Only valid for response obtained from `ClientRequest`.
.TP
\fBstatusMessage()\fR
The HTTP response status message (reason phrase). Such as "OK" or "Internal Server Error." Only valid for response obtained from `ClientRequest`.
.TP
\fBstatus()\fR
An alias for `statusCode`
.TP
\fBstatusText()\fR
An alias for `statusMessage`
.TP
\fBsendDate()\fR
If `true`, the "Date" header will be automatically generated and sent in the response if it is not already present in the headers. Defaults to `true`.
.TP
\fBwriteHead(statusCode, statusMessage, headers)\fR
Writes the response header to the request. The `statusCode` is a 3\-digit HTTP status code, like 200 or 404. The last argument, `headers`, are the response headers. Optionally one can give a human\-readable `statusMessage` as the second argument.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIstatusCode\fR (number \\| string; required)
.br
\fIstatusMessage\fR (string \\| object \\| string[]; optional; default null)
.br
\fIheaders\fR (object \\| string[]; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIClientRequest\fR
.TP
\fBend(chunk, encoding, callback)\fR
Finishes the server response.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIchunk\fR (Buffer \\| Uint8Array \\| string \\| function; optional; default null)
.br
\fIencoding\fR (string \\| function; optional; default null)
.br
\fIcallback\fR (function; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIOutgoingMessage\fR
.TP
\fBAgentOptions\fR
An options object container for an `Agent` instance.
.TP
\fBAgent (extends EventEmitter)\fR
An Agent is responsible for managing connection persistence and reuse for HTTP clients.
.TP
\fBconstructor(options)\fR
`Agent` class constructor.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (AgentOptions; optional; default null)
.TP
\fBcreateConnection(options, callback)\fR
Produces a socket/stream to be used for HTTP requests.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (object; required)
.br
\fIcallback\fR (function(Duplex); optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIDuplex\fR
.TP
\fBglobalAgent\fR
The global and default HTTP agent.
.TP
\fBConnection (extends Duplex)\fR
A duplex stream between a HTTP request `IncomingMessage` and the response `ServerResponse`
.TP
\fBclose()\fR
Closes the connection, destroying the underlying duplex, request, and response streams.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIConnection\fR
.TP
\fBServer (extends EventEmitter)\fR
A nodejs compat HTTP server typically intended for running in a "worker" environment.
.TP
\fBclosed()\fR
`true` if the server is closed, otherwise `false`.
.TP
\fBhost()\fR
The host to listen to. This value can be `null`. Defaults to `location.hostname`. This value is used to filter requests by hostname.
.TP
\fBport()\fR
The `port` to listen on. This value can be `0`, which is the default. This value is used to filter requests by port, if given. A port value of `0` does not filter on any port.
.TP
\fBconnections()\fR
A readonly array of all active or inactive (idle) connections.
.TP
\fBlistening()\fR
`true` if the server is listening for requests.
.TP
\fBmaxConnections()\fR
The number of concurrent max connections this server should handle. Default: Infinity
.TP
\fBaddress()\fR
Gets the HTTP server address and port that it this server is listening (emulated) on in the runtime with respect to the adapter internal being used by the server.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fI{ family: string, address: string, port: number}\fR
.TP
\fBclose(close)\fR
Closes the server.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIclose\fR (function; optional)
.TP
\fBcloseAllConnections()\fR
Closes all connections.
.TP
\fBcloseIdleConnections()\fR
Closes all idle connections.
.TP
\fBlisten(port, host, unused, callback)\fR
Documented method exposed by this module.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIport\fR (number \\| object; optional; default 0)
.br
\fIhost\fR (string; optional; default null)
.br
\fIunused\fR (function \\| null; optional; default null)
.br
\fIcallback\fR (function; optional)
.TP
\fBget(optionsOrURL, options, callback)\fR
Makes a HTTP or `oro:` GET request. A simplified alias to `request()`.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptionsOrURL\fR (string \\| object; required)
.br
\fIoptions\fR (object \\| function; optional)
.br
\fIcallback\fR (function; optional)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIClientRequest\fR
.TP
\fBcreateServer(options, callback)\fR
Creates a HTTP server that can listen for incoming requests. Requests that are dispatched to this server depend on the context in which it is created, such as a service worker which will use a "fetch event" adapter.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (object \\| function; optional; default null)
.br
\fIcallback\fR (function; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIServer\fR
